stranger things big bad wekner has  joined the ranks of tv and films great  iconic horror villains but as scary as  he already is there were a ton of even  more terrifying designs and looks that  didn't make the final cut yupi kai movie  lovers i'm jan and in this video i'm  revealing and explaining all the  horrifying bechner designs you never got  to see in the show this early version of  vetena had an armored shell over his  body and face and was inspired by the  prehistoric fish the dunkleosteus this  giant fish which was up to 29 feet long  and could weigh over four tons had large  bony plates that formed its face and  jaws and like wechner was a fearsome  predator the idea behind this original  design was that over time living in the  upside down had hardened and separated  pieces of henry's skin from each other  forming these tough plates over his body  another iteration of this design used a  spiky version of the armor which almost  gives them the appearance of being  covered in shards of rock or stone the  designs ended up being rejected as they  were too rigid and didn't allow for  enough of vectors expressions and  emotions to come through  this next early design had some  grotesque insect-like arms and legs the  look was inspired by the real-life  mantis and its two large four legs which  have adapted so that the creature can  catch and grab its prey the arms of this  particular vector could also split open  to form claws that he would then use to  stab his victims something vechna  actually did in his final form but with  his more human-like claws it's a very  creepy design that would have fit well  with henry creel's love of spiders and  it also reminds me of pennywise's spider  form in it chapter 2. the issue with it  though was that it would have been very  hard to achieve practically given the  extended appendages needed for the  villain the duffer brothers were keen  that that can have a practical feel  about him and the final version of the  villain was all practical makeup and  prosthetics with just vfx used for his  vines  this alternate version of wekner is much  more alien-like with some kind of skin  or webbing growing over and covering his  eyes making him appear almost blind the  thinking behind this look was to give  wekner more of an extraterrestrial vibe  with the idea being that henry's time in  the upside down had transformed him into  something closer to a demogorgon than a  human according to the artist michael  maher jr his look also reminds me of the  pale manned villain from pan's labyrinth  who eats children akin to wekner who  targets teenagers in season four  another early idea for wekner's look was  to have a patchwork of skin stretched  over his gaunt body the idea was  inspired by hellraiser and i think what  they were going for was the antagonist  frank who comes back from the dead in a  degenerated state until his body begins  to grow back flesh and skin as he  consumes his victims  an even more gruesome version of this  idea gave wekner extra pale skin like a  vampire which seems fitting given the  introduction of the demo bats in season  four and his teeth and mouth in this  design gives me some real cellobite  chatter revives from the hellraiser  franchise and there's a touch of the  demon of the mind elegos from ash vs the  evil dead in this design too these  designs were inspired by the idea that  because henry had been living in the  upside down for so long his skin had  begun to rot away falling apart in  patches with him clamping the skin  together to save it in an extra gross  version the skin hung over vacna's jaw  and in another the skin had melted over  his eyes and in this design whenever  wekner used his powers his eyes would  cry blood similar to what we see happens  to vacuna's victims the multiple eyes in  this design also remind me of henry and  his love of spiders creatures which  typically have many eyes all these  designs were rejected because similar to  the problem with wekner's armored skin  they didn't allow for enough expression  another idea that was initially explored  was for henry to become infected with a  type of gangrene that would corrupt his  body the thinking was that after years  of living in the upside down a mouldy  type of rot together with vines had  taken hold of henry's body and the  artist describes it as a type of  tumorous gangrene that would eat away at  wekner's flesh these designs followed a  similar idea the difference being that  the rot on wechner's body was a bit  brighter coloured and was a type of  radioactive rot that henry had caught  from his exposure to the upside down  although these looks were suitably scary  for the villain the designs were  discarded because they didn't disguise  wekner's true identity this was crucial  so that it would be more difficult to  immediately realize that the seemingly  friendly orderly that eleven first meets  at hawkins lab is actually the series  big bad  this alternate design for vechna  emphasizes his asymmetrical look with  his oversized left arm but with also a  giant tentacle attached a particularly  weird unused design is this one where  vacna still had some thin long strands  of hair on his head an idea that was  quickly rejected in all the subsequent  designs this vector also has some little  spikes growing out of his shoulders and  hands and the look of his face reminds  me a little of the serial killer from  the movie smiley i think it's safe to  say that most of these alternate designs  for vechna are even more terrifying and  unsettling than the already scary  version of the villain we did get in the  end the more humanoid version they went  for reflects his human origins better  together with the elements of the upside  down that became part of his body such  as roots vines and new muscle tissue  veteran has red purple and black colors  which are associated with the upside  down are meant to show how the alternate  dimension took over his body and any  human flesh left over is pale because  he's been away from daylight for such a  long time i do want to thank emmy  nominated artist michael marr junior for  sharing all of these incredible and  original designs for wekner which barry  gower and his makeup effects company  translated into an amazing on-screen  look for the villain the prosthetic  makeup took between six and seven hours  every day to apply meaning that the  makeup team and actor jamie campbell  bowers working day began at two or three  am so he'd be ready for shooting later  that morning and it then took another  hour once filming was finished each day  to take it all off all in all henry juan  and veckner make an incredibly  compelling central villain in stranger  things and if you'd like to learn how i  expect the series to end tap here to  watch my season 5 theory video and also  why 11 will end up using time travel to  defeat wekner there's also links in the  video description so movie lovers what  do you think of these alternate wekner  designs let me know in the comments  below if you liked this video do leave a  thumbs up i really appreciate it and you  can tap left to discover every  incredible easter egg you missed in the  final part of season 4. thanks for  enjoying stranger things with me and  hope you have a marvellous movie loving  week yippie kai movie lovers
 

